c['result'][0]='Let R_hyb be the unique root in (3/2,151/100) of R⁶ − 8R⁵ + 22R⁴ − 30R³ + 21R² − 6R + 1. There exists one fitness-independent sequence of finite connected loopless undirected weighted graphs G_t such that, for every fixed 1 < r < R_hyb, there exists t₀(r) for which every t ≥ t₀(r) strictly amplifies uniformly initialized single-mutant fixation under each pure Bd and dB process. Each comparison uses the complete graph on the same n_t vertices and the matching update rule. Hence R_sim ≥ R_hyb = 1.5028569127905696… > 3/2.'
c['result'].insert(1,'Bd chooses a fitness-weighted parent and then an edge-weighted replacement target. dB first chooses a uniformly random death site and then a neighboring parent with probability proportional to fitness times edge weight. Their finite complete-graph baselines differ: ρ_Bd(K_n,r) = (1−r⁻¹)/(1−r⁻ⁿ), whereas ρ_dB(K_n,r) = ((n−1)/n)(1−r⁻¹)/(1−r⁻⁽ⁿ⁻¹⁾). Initialization is uniform over all vertices, with exactly one mutant and resident fitness one.')
