c['limitations'][0]='The construction uses finite connected loopless undirected weighted graphs, uniform initialization of exactly one mutant, resident fitness one, a fixed mutant fitness r > 1, and the two specified pure Bd and dB rules. No guarantee is supplied for arbitrary initialization, directed or unweighted constructions, empirical evolutionary dynamics, or a process that randomly mixes the update rules.'
c['limitations'][2]='For the unrestricted simultaneous-amplification threshold R_sim, the result is a lower bound. Exact optimality applies only to fixed positive σ and λ in the displayed first-order dilute pair–pendant response model. It does not establish optimality over all growing graph families, singular or size-dependent parameter choices, other modules, or higher-order boundary gains. This work supplies no universal upper bound.'
